<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
    The day the next claim pays for. Ringed, not filled - it has not been earned yet, and filling it would say it had.

    THE STRIP'S RULE: state is carried by FILL WEIGHT, reward type by TEXT
    COLOUR. It used to carry both in the fill - a day already claimed was a
    solid warm block and a day that pays Stars was a gold-tinted one - so a
    lit cell was ambiguous: reached, or valuable? Now the box only ever says
    where you are in the week, and the label only ever says what the day pays.
-->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:shape="rectangle">
    <solid android:color="@android:color/transparent" />
    <stroke android:width="1dp" android:color="@color/text_wisp" />
    <corners android:radius="10dp" />
</shape>
